# The creed, enforced rather than promised. `default-src 'none'` denies every
# fetch this page could make, and what is named below is the whole of what it
# is allowed to reach: this host, one relay, and four services that answer with
# pictures of weather.
#
# Unlike Oikos, this instrument does leave the origin, and the list is the
# honest statement of where. Tiles arrive through `fetch` rather than through an
# `<img>` (see field.js: the watermark and the exception body are headers and a
# content type, which an image element cannot see), so they are connect-src and
# not img-src.
#
#   view.eumetsat.int      is absent on purpose: EUMETSAT sends no CORS header,
#                          so those two dishes are proxied by functions/msg.js
#                          and arrive as 'self'.
#   tilecache.rainviewer   is where api.rainviewer.com's index points today. It
#                          is returned by the API rather than fixed, so if the
#                          radar layer ever goes quiet with a console full of
#                          CSP refusals, that is what moved.
#   keraunos-relay         is VITE_FEED_URL. A different deploy, a different
#                          line: this file is static and cannot read the env.
#
# The hash is of the medium script in the head, which is inline because it has
# to run before first paint and cannot afford a round trip. Edit that script and
# recompute:
#   python3 -c "import re,hashlib,base64;s=re.search(r'<script>(.*?)</script>',open('index.html').read(),re.S).group(1);print(base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).digest()).decode())"
